<title>OMAN: Oman, Yemen sign international border maps.</title>
<headline>Oman, Yemen sign international border maps.</headline>
<dateline>MUSCAT 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oman and Yemen on Monday signed final copies of maps defining their international border, the official Omani news agency said.</p>
<p>The two Arabian peninsula countries signed a border accord in October 1992, ending a 25-year dispute over the 308 km (180 miles) frontier. A year later, they opened their first border crossing after the frontier was surveyed and new maps were printed.</p>
